ManiaScope
==========

ManiaScope and its difficulty model (skill_calc.py and the rest) are original work,
MIT-licensed — see LICENSE. No third-party calculator code is included or ported.

Ideas (not code) that informed the model: per-hand finger-state analysis and LN
layering (Quaver.API, MPL-2.0), per-column strain and fixed-time section aggregation
(osu!, MIT), hand-specific demand and stamina adjustment (Etterna MinaCalc).

The separate offline replay diagnostic (calib/replay_review.py) follows osu!lazer's
judgement-window, note-lock, hold-release and replay-bitmask semantics, informed
by ppy/osu commit f5f9e91be6ca6097caa3aa6473f24abd02ccb670 (MIT):
https://github.com/ppy/osu/tree/f5f9e91be6ca6097caa3aa6473f24abd02ccb670/osu.Game.Rulesets.Mania
Those upstream portions are Copyright (c) ppy Pty Ltd <contact@ppy.sh>; the MIT
permission and warranty terms in LICENSE apply. No upstream calculator or full
gameplay engine is bundled. Reconstruction discrepancies are reported explicitly.

Automatic rate tracking talks to tosu (https://github.com/tosuapp/tosu, LGPL-3.0)
over its local HTTP API. tosu is a separate program, downloaded by setup.sh from its
official releases and not distributed with ManiaScope.

osu! and osu!lazer are trademarks of their respective owners; ManiaScope is an
unaffiliated, third-party tool.
